<title>MEXICO: Mexico oil workers demand less private contracting.</title>
<headline>Mexico oil workers demand less private contracting.</headline>
<byline>Timna Tanners</byline>
<dateline>CADEREYTA, Mexico 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Oil workers at Mexico's celebrations of its 59th petroleum expropriation anniversary on Tuesday asked the government to cut back on private contracting in the industry.</p>
<p>Arguing the country's own oil workers are better equiped to handle such special projects, the mighty oil workers union leader Carlos Romero Deschamps told President Ernesto Zedillo that private contracting for state oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) projects is hurting the workers.</p>
</text>
